# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics has been successfully verified and configured for this Next.js project. The project already had the proper setup in place, following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## What Was Found
The project already had the complete and correct Vercel Web Analytics implementation:

### 1. Package Installation ✓
- `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 is listed in package.json dependencies
- Package is now properly installed in node_modules

### 2. Analytics Component Configuration ✓
- The Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next` is imported in `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Component is placed correctly in the `<body>` tag of the root layout
- Implementation matches the official Next.js App Router documentation exactly

### 3. Files Verified
- `web/package.json` - Contains @vercel/analytics@2.0.1 in dependencies
- `web/src/app/layout.tsx` - Properly imports and renders `<Analytics />` component

## Implementation Details

The existing implementation in `src/app/layout.tsx` follows best practices:
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This setup provides:
- Cookieless page view tracking
- Automatic Next.js route support
- Seamless integration with Vercel's Analytics dashboard
- No cookie banner requirements

